---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Header from '../components/Header.astro'
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Child Safety Standards - Ocean Dating App"
  description="Ocean's standards and policies against child sexual abuse and exploitation (CSAE)."
>
  <Header />
  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="container">
        <h1>Child Safety Standards</h1>
        <p>Our commitment to protecting minors and preventing exploitation</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="container">
        <div style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
          <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; opacity: 0.8;">
            Last updated: March 2026
          </p>

          <div style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
            <p style="line-height: 1.8; opacity: 0.9;">
              Crystal Dating, Inc. ("Ocean") is committed to maintaining a safe platform that
              protects minors and prevents child sexual abuse and exploitation (CSAE). This
              document outlines our policies, technical safeguards, and enforcement mechanisms
              to prevent the presence of minors on our platform and the sharing of illegal content.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
            <h2 style="font-size: 1.8rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">1. Age Verification and Eligibility</h2>

            <h3 style="font-size: 1.4rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Minimum Age Requirement</h3>
            <p style="line-height: 1.8; opacity: 0.9;">
              Ocean is exclusively for adults 18 years of age and older. All users must provide
              their date of birth during account registration. Accounts cannot be created by
              individuals under 18 years of age.
            </p>

            <h3 style="font-size: 1.4rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 1rem;">Age Verification Process</h3>
            <ul style="line-height: 1.8; opacity: 0.9;">
              <li>Date of birth is required during sign-up and validated against the minimum age requirement</li>
              <li>Users who do not meet the age requirement are prevented from creating an account</li>
              <li>Age verification is mandatory and cannot be bypassed</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 style="font-size: 1.4rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 1rem;">Terms of Service Violation</h3>
            <p style="line-height: 1.8; opacity: 0.9;">
              Being under 18 years of age is a direct violation of our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>.
              Any accounts found to belong to minors will be immediately terminated and permanently deleted.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
            <h2 style="font-size: 1.8rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">2. User Reporting Mechanisms</h2>

            <p style="line-height: 1.8; opacity: 0.9;">
              We empower our community to help maintain platform safety through comprehensive
              reporting tools.
            </p>

            <h3 style="font-size: 1.4rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 1rem;">Report Suspected Minors</h3>
            <p style="line-height: 1.8; opacity: 0.9;">
              Users can report other users whom they suspect may be under 18 years of age.
              All reports are reviewed by our safety team, and appropriate action is taken,
              including account investigation, suspension, and permanent removal.
            </p>

            <h3 style="font-size: 1.4rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 1rem;">Report Review Process</h3>
            <ul style="line-height: 1.8; opacity: 0.9;">
              <li>All reports of suspected minors are reviewed promptly by trained moderators</li>
              <li>Reported accounts may be immediately suspended pending investigation</li>
              <li>Confirmed violations result in permanent account deletion</li>
              <li>Repeat violators and those attempting to circumvent age restrictions are permanently banned</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
            <h2 style="font-size: 1.8rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">3. Content Moderation and Safety Controls</h2>

            <h3 style="font-size: 1.4rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Profile Image Moderation</h3>
            <p style="line-height: 1.8; opacity: 0.9;">
              Users can upload images to their profile. To prevent the sharing of explicit or
              inappropriate content:
            </p>
            <ul style="line-height: 1.8; opacity: 0.9;">
              <li>All uploaded images are automatically scanned using AI-powered nudity detection technology</li>
              <li>Images containing nudity or sexually explicit content are automatically rejected and deleted</li>
              <li>Images are scanned before being made visible to other users</li>
              <li>Users who repeatedly attempt to upload prohibited content may have their accounts suspended or terminated</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 style="font-size: 1.4rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 1rem;">Messaging Restrictions</h3>
            <p style="line-height: 1.8; opacity: 0.9;">
              To prevent the sharing of explicit or illegal content through private communications:
            </p>
            <ul style="line-height: 1.8; opacity: 0.9;">
              <li>Users can message other matched users through text-based messaging</li>
              <li>Image sharing is not permitted in messages, eliminating a common vector for CSAE material</li>
              <li>Messages may be reviewed by our moderation team if reported by users</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
            <h2 style="font-size: 1.8rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">4. Enforcement and Cooperation</h2>

            <h3 style="font-size: 1.4rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Zero Tolerance Policy</h3>
            <p style="line-height: 1.8; opacity: 0.9;">
              Ocean maintains a zero-tolerance policy for child exploitation, abuse, or the
              presence of minors on our platform. Violations result in:
            </p>
            <ul style="line-height: 1.8; opacity: 0.9;">
              <li>Immediate and permanent account termination</li>
              <li>Deletion of all user data associated with the account</li>
              <li>Permanent ban preventing future account creation</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 style="font-size: 1.4rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 1rem;">Law Enforcement Cooperation</h3>
            <p style="line-height: 1.8; opacity: 0.9;">
              We cooperate fully with law enforcement agencies investigating child exploitation
              and abuse. We comply with all applicable legal requirements, including:
            </p>
            <ul style="line-height: 1.8; opacity: 0.9;">
              <li>Reporting suspected child sexual abuse material (CSAM) to the National Center for Missing & Exploited Children (NCMEC) as required by law</li>
              <li>Preserving evidence and providing information to law enforcement pursuant to valid legal requests</li>
              <li>Working with authorities to identify and prosecute offenders</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
            <h2 style="font-size: 1.8rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">5. Ongoing Safety Improvements</h2>
            <p style="line-height: 1.8; opacity: 0.9;">
              We continuously evaluate and improve our safety measures to better protect our
              community and prevent exploitation. This includes:
            </p>
            <ul style="line-height: 1.8; opacity: 0.9;">
              <li>Regular review and enhancement of our content moderation systems</li>
              <li>Updates to detection algorithms to identify prohibited content and behavior</li>
              <li>Training for moderation teams on emerging threats and best practices</li>
              <li>Collaboration with industry partners and safety organizations</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
            <h2 style="font-size: 1.8rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">6. Resources and Support</h2>

            <h3 style="font-size: 1.4rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Reporting Concerns</h3>
            <p style="line-height: 1.8; opacity: 0.9;">
              If you encounter a suspected minor on the platform or observe any concerning
              behavior related to child safety:
            </p>
            <ul style="line-height: 1.8; opacity: 0.9;">
              <li>Use the in-app reporting feature to report the user immediately</li>
              <li>Contact our safety team at <a href="mailto:safety@oceandating.app">safety@oceandating.app</a></li>
            </ul>

            <h3 style="font-size: 1.4rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 1rem;">External Resources</h3>
            <p style="line-height: 1.8; opacity: 0.9;">
              If you believe a child is in immediate danger, contact local law enforcement
              or call the National Child Abuse Hotline at 1-800-4-A-CHILD (1-800-422-4453).
            </p>
            <p style="line-height: 1.8; opacity: 0.9;">
              To report child sexual abuse material (CSAM) online, you can also file a report
              directly with NCMEC at <a href="https://report.cybertip.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">report.cybertip.org</a>.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 style="font-size: 1.8rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">7. Contact Us</h2>
            <p style="line-height: 1.8; opacity: 0.9;">
              For questions about our child safety standards or to report safety concerns:
            </p>
            <p style="line-height: 1.8; opacity: 0.9; margin-top: 1rem;">
              <strong>Crystal Dating, Inc.</strong><br />
              Safety Team<br />
              3229 Greenpoint Ave PMB 107<br />
              Long Island City, NY 11101<br />
              United States<br />
              Email: <a href="mailto:support@oceandating.app">support@oceandating.app</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
